---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BADGE_YEAR, EARNED_TIERS, RANK_CUTOFF, badgesFor } from '../../lib/badge';

/**
 * What the badge means, and the two rules that come with it.
 *
 * Every other directory in this business sells its badge, or sells the placement the badge
 * announces. The page has to say plainly that this one is free, because a reader's first
 * assumption will be the opposite, and it has to say what we keep: the link back, and the right
 * to stop serving a badge the firm no longer qualifies for.
 *
 * The counts are read from the directory rather than typed, for the same reason every other
 * number on this site is.
 */
const firms = await getCollection('firms', f =>
  f.data.status !== 'sample' && f.data.status !== 'not_eligible');

const tiers = new Map<string, number>();
let ranked = 0;
let firmsWithAny = 0;
for (const f of firms) {
  const badges = badgesFor(f, firms);
  if (badges.length) firmsWithAny += 1;
  ranked += badges.filter(b => !b.kind.startsWith('tier')).length;
  const tier = f.data.score?.tier;
  if (tier && EARNED_TIERS.includes(tier)) tiers.set(tier, (tiers.get(tier) ?? 0) + 1);
}
const order = ['Elite', 'Distinguished', 'Certified', 'Verified'];
const tierRows = order.filter(t => tiers.get(t)).map(t => ({ tier: t, n: tiers.get(t)! }));
const earned = tierRows.reduce((n, r) => n + r.n, 0);

const example = firms.find(f => f.data.slug === 'goodwin-law-pa') ?? firms[0];
const exampleBadges = badgesFor(example, firms);
---
<Base title="The LFL badge"
      description="What the Law Firm Listings badge means, who has earned one, and the two rules that come with it. Free, never for sale, rebuilt every time we re-measure."
      nav="methodology">
<section class="page-hero on-night">
  <div class="aurora" aria-hidden="true"><i class="b1"></i><i class="b2"></i><i class="b3"></i></div>
  <div class="container">
    <div>
      <ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">The badge</li></ol>
      <span class="eyebrow">Yours to display</span>
      <h1>The badge is free, and it is not for sale.</h1>
      <p class="lede">{earned.toLocaleString('en-US')} firms have earned a tier and
        {' '}{firmsWithAny.toLocaleString('en-US')} have at least one badge to show for it. Nobody
        paid for one, nobody can, and the fastest way to get one is to publish more about your
        own firm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-facts">
      {tierRows.map(r => (
        <div class="fact"><b class="num">{r.n}</b><span>{r.tier}</span></div>
      ))}
      <div class="fact"><b class="num">{ranked}</b><span>Ranking badges</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="narrow prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">Two kinds</span>
    <h2 style="margin-top:14px">One says what we measured. The other says where you placed.</h2>
    <p>The Certification Score is computed for a firm, not for one of its practice areas, so the
      tier badge names no practice. It reads <b>LFL {example.data.score?.tier ?? 'Verified'} {BADGE_YEAR}</b>
      and it means the gates were checked and the score computed from public records.</p>
    <p>Position is a different measurement and a narrower one. A ranking is scoped to a city and
      a practice, so a ranking badge can name both, and it says the whole thing: not "top ten"
      but <b>ranked {' '}{exampleBadges[1]?.headline.replace('Ranked ', '').split(' ·')[0] ?? '1st of 20'}</b>,
      with the size of the field in it. A firm in the first {RANK_CUTOFF} of a ranking earns one,
      every year, for every ranking it is in.</p>
    <p>{example.data.name} is why the two are separate. It is first of twenty for real estate in
      Naples and its tier is Verified rather than Certified. Both are true. A single badge saying
      "Certified in Real Estate" would be neither, and we would have made it up.</p>

    <h2>The two rules</h2>
    <p><b>Link it back.</b> The badge has to link to your profile on this site, because the point
      of it is that somebody can check. An award nobody can verify is decoration.</p>
    <p><b>Do not edit the file.</b> Hotlink it from this domain rather than saving a copy. That
      is not about bandwidth. The file is rebuilt every time we re-measure, so the badge on your
      site keeps telling the truth on its own: if your tier changes, it changes, and if you stop
      qualifying it stops being served. Everyone else in this industry hands out a picture that
      says the same thing for ever. That is exactly the difference we are selling.</p>

    <h2>What it costs</h2>
    <p>Nothing, and there is no version that costs something. The annual listing on
      {' '}<a href="/list-your-firm/">/list-your-firm/</a> buys a followed link, your logo and the
      reviews you want quoted. It does not buy a badge, a point, a gate, a tier or a position,
      and the firms above paid for none of this.</p>

    <h2>How to get yours</h2>
    <p>Open your own profile and look for <b>Show this on your site</b>. The badge, both colour
      versions and the code to paste are all there. If your firm is listed and you cannot find
      the section, you have not earned one yet, and the profile says which gate is open.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">An example</span>
    <h2 style="margin:14px 0 22px">{example.data.name}</h2>
    <div class="badge-grid">
      {exampleBadges.slice(0, 2).map(b => (
        <div class="badge-offer">
          <img src={`/badge/${example.data.slug}/${b.kind}.svg`} alt={b.alt}
               width="310" height="96" loading="lazy" />
          <div>
            <b>{b.headline}</b>
            <p class="muted" style="font-size:.88rem;margin-top:6px">Also in a
              {' '}<a class="link" href={`/badge/${example.data.slug}/${b.kind}-light.svg`}>light version</a>
              {' '}for a pale background.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:.9rem;margin-top:20px">
      <a class="link" href={`/firms/${example.data.slug}/`}>See the profile these link to</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
